### **Implementation Summary**

#### **1. Default Value Adjustment for `terminalBuffer` / `ui.terminalBuffer`**
* Changed default value of `terminalBuffer` to `false` to avoid performance regressions with very long chat histories outside of alternate shell environments:
  * [settingsSchema.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/test_large_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_24874/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/config/settingsSchema.ts)
  * [config.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/test_large_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_24874/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/core/src/config/config.ts)
  * [settings.schema.json](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/test_large_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_24874/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/schemas/settings.schema.json)

#### **2. Interactive UI Render Process Control**
* Updated package rendering logic in [interactiveCli.tsx](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/test_large_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_24874/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/interactiveCli.tsx) so `renderProcess` is only active when both `config.getUseRenderProcess()` and `config.getUseTerminalBuffer()` evaluate to `true`.

#### **3. Conditional Alternative Buffer Handling in `InputPrompt`**
* Updated rendering flow in [InputPrompt.tsx](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/test_large_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_24874/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/components/InputPrompt.tsx):
  * **When `isAlternateBuffer` is true**: Continue utilizing virtualized scrolling `ScrollableList` for efficiency.
  * **When `isAlternateBuffer` is false**: Render a precise slice of `scrollableData` directly using `React.Fragment` elements to prevent empty page rendering artifacts.

#### **4. Conditional alternative Buffer Handling in `ToolResultDisplay`**
* Standardized ANSI array outputs rendering flow in [ToolResultDisplay.tsx](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/test_large_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_24874/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/components/messages/ToolResultDisplay.tsx):
  * **When `isAlternateBuffer` is true**: Render virtualized scrolling with `ScrollableList`.
  * **When `isAlternateBuffer` is false**: Calculate the slice of visible lines and total hidden lines, and render with `MaxSizedBox` and `AnsiLineText` to avoid artifact gaps.

#### **5. Truncation Retention**
* Adjusted the condition in [MaxSizedBox.tsx](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/test_large_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_24874/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/components/shared/MaxSizedBox.tsx) from `if (effectiveMaxHeight === undefined)` to `if (effectiveMaxHeight === undefined && totalHiddenLines === 0)` so truncation indicators continue to render correctly even if there's no explicitly defined maxHeight.

